## Context

The 0439 master pass absorbed four "extension" rows as UNITS of their parent
plant (`Duyen Hai 3 Extension` → unit of Duyen Hai 3; same for `Uong Bi I
extension`, `Uong Bi II extension`, `Vinh Tan 4 extension`). During the 0413 v2
adoption the author observed this was an uninformed choice and asked whether it
only increased errors.

Measured during 0413 (one side of the ledger only): absorption added **15 new
false positives** — model emissions of the extension names are now LP-vetoed
against the absorbed parent (the `matcher_fail_lp_veto` jump in
`fp_audit_exp2.py`, full v1→v2 audit in `data/reference/v1_v2_adoption_comparison.md`).

But absorption is **also** the entire mechanism behind the clean +212 TP /
−212 FP gain and the parent capacity corrections (Duyen Hai 3 1244→1904 =
parent + ext, etc.). So "did it only increase errors?" cannot be answered from
the FP column alone — the honest measurement is **net** TP/FP/FN across both
arms. This was deliberately NOT done in 0413: changing what the pipe produces is
a master/aggregator decision (0439/0416), not the adoption ceremony, and a
revert mid-adoption would re-run the entire 0413 gate (count 170→174,
v1↔v2 accounting, every figure, the re-score).

## Approach

1. Build a **standalone-extensions variant** of the v2 reference: the 4
   extensions become standalone one-unit plants instead of absorbed units
   (count 170→174, parents lose the ext capacity). Do this in the MASTER
   (`pipeline.ods` Plant/Unit address cells) + re-run the pipe, NOT by hand-editing
   the CSV — parentage is data, not a name inference (0439 contract).
2. Re-score Exp1 (exp1_batch2) under both variants from existing archived
   outputs (LP matcher, zero API spend) and compare **aggregate TP / FP / FN**,
   not just FP. Decision rule: adopt whichever variant has the lower net error
   (FP + FN) on the reference, holding TP recall in view.
3. If standalone wins: it becomes the v2 reference (new version entry in
   PROVENANCE, before/after gate against current v2, re-score, figures). If
   absorbed wins: document the measurement as the justification and keep current
   v2 — the choice is then informed, not accidental.

## Definition of done

- [ ] Standalone-extensions variant produced via the master + pipe (not a hand
      edit); count and per-plant capacity diffs vs absorbed documented.
- [ ] Exp1 re-scored under both variants; net TP/FP/FN compared in a committed
      note under `data/reference/`.
- [ ] Decision recorded with the measurement as evidence (no loaded causal
      label — report the net effect, not "absorption broke scoring").
- [ ] If reverted: PROVENANCE version entry + before/after gate + figures
      regenerated, same discipline as 0413.
- [ ] The final adopted plant count is settled (this is the count the
      `\NumRefPlants` macro and all manuscript reference-size mentions resolve
      to — see 0444 macroization, blocked on this).
- [ ] `make check` green.

